  m_Name: FW_JoyDivision
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FotowandData
  photo: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b7dd11023c3b1e748aae395dc30b41c4, type: 3}
  title: "Joy Division \u2013 On Tour, Kant Kino Berlin, 21 Januar"
  description: 'A concert poster for Joy Division ''on Tour'', performing Monday

    21
    January at Kant Kino, Berlin, 20:00. The poster features the

    now-iconic
    pulsar wave graphic from their debut album

    ''Unknown Pleasures''.'
  hasExtraInfo: 1
  extraInfoTitle: Joy Division in Berlin
  extraInfoContent: "Joy Division's January 1980 Berlin concert at Kant Kino\ncame
    during a period of intense creativity for the band,\njust before the release
    of their second album 'Closer'.\nWest Berlin held a special significance for
    the post-punk\ngeneration \u2014 its isolation, tension, and vibrant underground\nscene
    made it a spiritual home for the dark, atmospheric\nsound Joy Division embodied.
    The poster's pulsar graphic,\ntaken from 'Unknown Pleasures', has since become\none
    of the most recognized images in music history.\nSinger Ian Curtis would die
    in May 1980, making this\none of the last documented records of the band performing
    in Berlin."
  extraInfoImage: {fileID: 0}
